// A float COMPUTATION has no Terminal route. A float copy does. Reduced while
// attributing the six-sample guard cluster; the repair is owned by
// OPERATOR-BOUNDARY-CALLS, which already records that compiler-known float
// realizations are absent. This is the reproduction, not a second claim on it.
//
//   main.d = main.e;                 (copy)         checks
//   main.flag = main.n > 5;          (integer cmp)  checks
//   main.d = main.d + main.e;        (float arith)  OMITTED
//   main.flag = main.d > 211.5;      (float cmp)    OMITTED
//   main.flag = main.d == main.e;    (float cmp)    OMITTED (this fixture)
//
// It is not about guards, which is what the cluster's shared phase suggests.
// Every position fails and each reports a different phase, none naming a
// float:
//
//   transition main.d > 211.5 { true -> .. _ -> .. }
//                          `state graph: terminator: conditional successors:
//                           guard expression`
//   transition { main.d > 211.5 -> .. _ -> .. }      the same
//   let b: bool = main.d > 211.5;
//                          `statement sequence: local data: scalar local:
//                           pure initializer`
//   main.flag = main.d > 211.5;
//                          `structural field store: pure source: scalar
//                           expression row`
//
// Binding the comparison to a local or a field first is therefore NOT a
// workaround; there is no spelling of a float computation that routes.
//
// What names the real owner: import `omega::language::core::float_operations`
// and the same comparison becomes a call, omitting at
// `a missing boundary target (\`Float::equal\`)`. Every operator and both
// widths behave alike -- `>`, `<`, `==` on `f64`, and `>` on `f32`.
//
// CLUSTER ATTRIBUTION, recorded here because the phase string hides it. The
// six samples reporting `state graph: terminator: conditional successors:
// guard expression` are TWO causes, three each:
//   float comparison guards -- cli/{arithmetic/dual_float,
//     basics/unit_converter, simulation/particle_sim}  -> this gap
//   `main.i < main.text.len` with `i: i32` against a u64 length --
//     cli/text/{parse_int,roman_numeral,string_hash}   -> already pinned at
//     tests/omega/pending/expressions/mixed_integer_guard_comparison
use omega_language_std::console;

data Main {
}

machine Main::main(main: &mut Main) reaches Console {
    let mut left: f64 = 212.0;
    let mut right: f64 = 2.0;
    let mut equal: bool = left == right;
    Console::exit_process(0);
}
